{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
        var_c += arg0;
        unresolved_70a08231[address(uint160(uint256(store_f)))] += arg0;
        emit Event_47374573(arg0, var_c);
    }","notes":"deposit(100) must succeed and credit the caller: reference balanceOf/totalSupply become 0x44b (1000 minted + 100) and getStats shows balance=totalSupply=0x44b, paused flag 0, fee 0x64, last 0. Candidate reverted (ok:false) because the unit ended in bare revert() and never wrote state. Removed the trailing revert, kept the paused/max checks (store_f paused byte is 0 after setup, arg0=100 >= store_c=1, so both pass), then added the accumulation: var_c (totalSupply, read by entrypoint_25/22) += arg0 and unresolved_70a08231[caller] += arg0 (read by balanceOf/getStats), plus the deposit event. The paused flag byte is only mutated by pause/unpause (entrypoint_8/9) which are untouched, and the max check still uses store_c as before, so the previously-exact deposit_above_max observation (arg < store_c reverting with CustomError_3261c792) is preserved."}
